WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:16.267
The day arrived to start our journey to visit the squire's friends.

2
00:00:17.608 --> 00:00:19.930
John and James hitched Ginger and me to the carriage.

3
00:00:22.751 --> 00:00:26.553
Then James drove us to the front doors of the house where the squire and his wife were

4
00:00:26.574 --> 00:00:30.616
waiting. They got in, and we were off.

5
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.921
We were on the road all day.

6
00:00:35.842 --> 00:00:39.584
There were some steep hills along the way, but James drove very carefully.

7
00:00:40.705 --> 00:00:43.047
And he always kept us on the smoothest part of the road.

8
00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:49.912
If the uphill was long, he turned the carriage to the side to let us rest for a

9
00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:53.554
moment. Ginger and I were grateful for his thoughtfulness.

10
00:00:54.535 --> 00:00:55.696
It made our job easier.

11
00:00:58.618 --> 00:01:01.280
Just as the sun was going down, we reached a town.

12
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.061
"We'll stop here for the night," the squire said.

13
00:01:05.081 --> 00:01:07.601
"Take us to the hotel, please, James."

14
00:01:07.621 --> 00:01:10.522
"Yes, sir," James said.

15
00:01:11.662 --> 00:01:15.904
He drove us through the streets and beneath an archway that led into the courtyard of a large

16
00:01:15.964 --> 00:01:22.165
hotel. We left the squire and his wife at the entrance, and then continued on to the stables

17
00:01:22.205 --> 00:01:22.705
at the back.

18
00:01:24.586 --> 00:01:26.146
A stable worker was waiting for us.

19
00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.967
He was a little old man with a crooked leg.

20
00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.408
But the leg didn't seem to bother him much.

21
00:01:33.568 --> 00:01:37.571
He was as active and lively as could be, rushing out to help James unhitch us.

22
00:01:38.993 --> 00:01:41.795
"What a beauty you are," he told me in a friendly voice.

23
00:01:42.355 --> 00:01:44.838
Let's get you cleaned up so you can rest, all right?"

24
00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.721
He led me into the stable.

25
00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:54.766
There were a number of stalls in there, with horses standing in several of them.

26
00:01:56.427 --> 00:01:57.848
Another worker brought Ginger in.

27
00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.912
He began to groom her while the little old man worked on me.

28
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.741
James watched them both carefully.

29
00:02:07.102 --> 00:02:10.923
I have never been groomed as lightly and expertly as I was by that little old man.

30
00:02:13.684 --> 00:02:16.225
When he finished, James ran his hands over me.

31
00:02:16.245 --> 00:02:18.967
"Wow," he said.

32
00:02:18.987 --> 00:02:23.989
"I thought I was fast at grooming a horse, and my boss John even faster.

33
00:02:25.249 --> 00:02:27.050
But you put us both to shame!"

34
00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:31.952
"Practice makes perfect," the old man said with a chuckle.

35
00:02:33.104 --> 00:02:34.885
"And I've had plenty of practice.

36
00:02:35.826 --> 00:02:37.868
I've been doing this for forty years!"

37
00:02:37.888 --> 00:02:39.949
"Forty years?"

38
00:02:40.309 --> 00:02:42.171
James said, sounding impressed.

39
00:02:42.191 --> 00:02:44.633
"That's a long time."

40
00:02:44.653 --> 00:02:47.955
"Yes, indeed," the old man agreed.

41
00:02:47.975 --> 00:02:51.197
"I started at age twelve.

42
00:02:52.198 --> 00:02:55.401
I've always been small, so I was a jockey for a while.

43
00:02:56.401 --> 00:02:59.724
But one day I was riding in a race when my horse slipped.

44
00:03:01.396 --> 00:03:05.218
I came off and broke my knee, and after that I couldn't ride anymore.

45
00:03:06.539 --> 00:03:10.421
But I couldn't live without horses, so I got a job at this hotel."

46
00:03:10.441 --> 00:03:14.704
"I can see that you do a good job here," James said.

47
00:03:14.724 --> 00:03:18.486
"Thank you, my boy," the old man said.

48
00:03:18.506 --> 00:03:24.229
"I enjoy it, especially when I get the chance to handle an animal like this one."

49
00:03:25.089 --> 00:03:25.730
He patted me.

50
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:31.650
"If you let me handle a horse for a few minutes, I can always tell you what sort

51
00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:32.650
of treatment he's had.

52
00:03:33.811 --> 00:03:38.275
And I can tell this black horse of yours is well-bred and was treated kindly."

53
00:03:41.398 --> 00:03:43.700
After that the old man put me in a stall and fed me.

54
00:03:45.301 --> 00:03:49.505
Ginger was in the stall beside me, and we were both glad to have a rest after our

55
00:03:49.565 --> 00:03:50.586
long day on the road.

56
00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:57.371
Later that evening a different worker came in to give us more hay and water.

57
00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.824
Horses stood in every stall by now, and he was busy taking care of us all.

58
00:04:04.766 --> 00:04:06.027
Then a young man wandered in.

59
00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:07.968
He was smoking a pipe.

60
00:04:07.988 --> 00:04:11.832
"Hello, Fowler," the worker greeted him.

61
00:04:11.852 --> 00:04:13.353
"Could you do me a favor?"

62
00:04:13.373 --> 00:04:16.196
"Sure, what is it?"

63
00:04:17.036 --> 00:04:19.278
The young man let out a puff of smoke from his pipe.

64
00:04:19.298 --> 00:04:25.404
"Climb up into the loft and toss down some more hay," the worker said.

65
00:04:26.388 --> 00:04:28.749
"But be sure to set down your pipe first."

66
00:04:28.769 --> 00:04:30.989
"All right."

67
00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.970
The young man hurried off out of sight.

68
00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.131
Just then James came into the stable to check on Ginger and me.

69
00:04:38.151 --> 00:04:42.672
"Everything looks fine here," he said, giving us each a pat.

70
00:04:42.692 --> 00:04:46.994
"Get some rest, and I'll see you in the morning."

71
00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:55.356
Shortly after he left, the stable went dark and quiet for the night.

72
00:04:57.648 --> 00:05:00.289
I ate a little more hay, and then drifted off to sleep.

73
00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:05.271
I awoke sometime later, feeling strangely uncomfortable.

74
00:05:06.192 --> 00:05:07.492
At first I wasn't sure why.

75
00:05:10.134 --> 00:05:11.274
I stood, coughing.

76
00:05:12.374 --> 00:05:13.955
A moment later Ginger coughed too.

77
00:05:14.996 --> 00:05:18.937
The air was thick with smoke, and a crackling sound came from the loft overhead.

78
00:05:21.258 --> 00:05:24.820
Suddenly there was a cry from somewhere outside: "Fire!"
